<title>USA: NBC beats CBS in Nielsen ratings.</title>
<headline>NBC beats CBS in Nielsen ratings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co unit NBC attracted the largest prime-time evening audience during the week of August 4 to August 10, Nielsen Media Research said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In second place was Westinghouse Electric Corp's CBS.</p>
<p>For the week ended Sunday:</p>
<p>-- NBC drew an average 7.4 rating, or percentage of America's roughly 97 million homes with television, and a 14 percent share of homes watching television during evening hours;</p>
<p>-- CBS won an average 6.9 rating, and a 13 percent share of homes watching television;</p>
<p>-- Walt Disney Co's ABC's average rating was 6.4 percent for the week and its shares was 12 percent;</p>
<p>-- News Corp's FOX had a 5.4 average rating and a share percentage of 10 percent;</p>
<p>-- UPN, a unit of Chris-Craft Industries Inc allied with Viacom Inc, had a 2.6 percent rating and a four percent share;</p>
<p>-- WB, a unit of Time Warner Inc, had a 2.3 percent rating and a four percent share.</p>
<p>(( -- Holly Rosenkrantz 212-859-1727 ))</p>
